From: zigzag go-port/rustcore
Subject: [PATCH 6] fix(latest_events): the listen task holds no strong Client

Client::latest_events() builds LatestEvents with SendQueue::new(self.clone()),
and LatestEvents::new moved that SendQueue into listen_to_updates_task, which
only calls subscribe() on it once, at its start. A SendQueue holds a strong
Client. The task's handle lives in ClientInner (latest_events) and aborts the
task when it drops — which never happens while the task holds a Client: a
reference cycle. Once a sync response subscribed a room's latest event
(sync::subscribe_to_room_latest_events, whenever the event cache is
subscribed), the Client, its tasks and its SQLite stores outlived every handle
the app held, for the life of the process.

- LatestEvents::new subscribes to the send queue and hands the task the
  receiver; the SendQueue (and its Client) is dropped when new() returns.

Upstreamable (generic, no app names).
---
diff --git a/crates/matrix-sdk/src/latest_events/mod.rs b/crates/matrix-sdk/src/latest_events/mod.rs
index a920208..519e38e 100644
--- a/crates/matrix-sdk/src/latest_events/mod.rs
+++ b/crates/matrix-sdk/src/latest_events/mod.rs
